{"title":"KVPY","category":"Engineering","bank":"kvpy","subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Continuity and Differentiability","count":10,"questions":[{"id":51607,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Continuity and Differentiability","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"For real $x$ with $-10 \\leq x \\leq 10$ define $f(x)=\\int_{-10}^{x} 2^{[t]} d t$, where for a real number $r$ we denote by $[r]$ the largest integer less than or equal to r. The number of points of discontinutiy of $\\mathrm{f}$ in the interval $(-10,10)$ is","options":["0","10","18","19"],"answer":0,"solution":"Let $r$ be an integer in $(-10,10)$\n\\begin{array}{l}\n\\text { Now, } L H L=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow r^{-}} \\int_{-10}^{x} 2^{[t]} d t \\\\\n=\\lim _{h \\rightarrow 0^{+}}\\left[\\int_{-10}^{-9} 2^{[t]} d t+\\int_{-9}^{-8} 2^{[t]} d t+\\ldots+\\int_{r-1}^{r-h} 2^{[t]} d t\\right] \\\\\n=\\lim _{h \\rightarrow 0}\\left[2^{-10}+2^{-9}+\\ldots . .+2^{r-1}(1-h)\\right] \\\\\n=2^{-10}+2^{-\\theta}+\\ldots+2^{n-1}..(1)\n\\end{array}\n\n\\begin{array}{l}\n\\lim _{x \\rightarrow r^{+}} \\int_{-10}^{x} 2^{[t]} d t \\\\\n=\\lim _{h \\rightarrow 0^{+}}\\left[\\int_{-10^{2}}^{-9} 2^{[t]} d t+\\int_{-9}^{-8} 2^{[t]} d t+\\ldots+\\int_{r}^{r+h} 2^{[t]} d t\\right] \\\\\n=2^{-10}+2^{-9}+\\ldots . .+2^{n-1}...(2) \\\\\nf(r)=\\int_{-10}^{r} 2^{[t]} d t \\\\\n=2^{-10}+2^{-9}+\\ldots+2^{-1}..(3)\n\\end{array}\n\nFrom $(1),(2) \\&(3)f(x)$ is continous-u : integers.\n$f(x)$ is continous at all integers.","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2013 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d213688ea7af70bd757f"},{"id":51608,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Continuity and Differentiability","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Define $\\mathrm{g}(\\mathrm{x})=\\int_{-3}^{3} \\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x}-\\mathrm{y}) \\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{y}) \\mathrm{dy}$, for all real $\\mathrm{x}$, where $f(t)=\\left\\{\\begin{array}{ll}1, & 0 \\leq t \\leq 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text { elsewhere }\\end{array}\\right.$\nThen","options":["$\\mathrm{g}(\\mathrm{x})$ is not continuous everywhere","$\\mathrm{g}(\\mathrm{x})$ is continuous everywhere but differentiable nowhere","$\\mathrm{g}(\\mathrm{x})$ is continuous everywhere and differentiable everywhere except at $\\mathrm{x}=0,1$","$g(x)$ is continuous everywhere and differentiable everywhere except at $\\mathrm{x}=0,1,2$"],"answer":3,"solution":"Definition can be break as\n$\\begin{array}{l}\ng(x)=\\int_{0}^{1} f(x-y) d y \\\\\nx-y=t ;-d y \\cdot d t \\\\\ng(x)=\\int_{x-1}^{x} f(t) d t \\\\\ng(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{array}{cc}\n0 & x \\leq 0 \\\\\nx & 0 \\lt  x \\lt  1 \\\\\n2-x & 1 \\leq x \\leq 2 \\\\\n0 & x\\gt 2\n\\end{array}\\right.\n\\end{array}$\nNow, check yourself","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2017 (5 Nov SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d213663b0ff1a278d533"},{"id":51609,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Continuity and Differentiability","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"For a real number $x$ let $[x]$ denote the largest number less than or equal to $x$. for $x \\in R$ let $f(x)=[x] \\sin \\pi x$. Then:","options":["$\\mathrm{f}$ is differentiable on $\\mathrm{R}$","$f$ is symmetric about the line $x=0$","$\\int_{-3}^{3} f(x) d x=0$","For each real $\\alpha$, the equation $f(x)-\\alpha=0$ has infinitely many roots."],"answer":3,"solution":"$f(x)=[x] \\sin \\pi x$\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fkvpy%252Fycnepzp4VDV-ROU6Tqvxr4Jv4lo4gzBcM8f6TcnUlsY.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2Fycnepzp4VDV-ROU6Tqvxr4Jv4lo4gzBcM8f6TcnUlsY.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2Fycnepzp4VDV-ROU6Tqvxr4Jv4lo4gzBcM8f6TcnUlsY.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2014 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d2131951650719911ba1"},{"id":51610,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Continuity and Differentiability","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be a function defined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi>if</mi><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn><mo> </mo><mi>if</mi><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p>Then, at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is</p>","options":["not continuous","continuous but not differentiable","differentiable and the derivative is not continuous","differentiable and the derivative is continuous"],"answer":3,"solution":"<p>Given function </p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"[\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>if</mi><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p>then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is continuous at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p>Now, for differentiability </p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>RHD</mi></math> (at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>)</p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>\n\n<p>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LHD</mi></math> (at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>)</p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>\n\n<p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is differentiable at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo> </mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>if</mi><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>if</mi><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∵</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is differentiable and the derivative is continuous.</p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2019 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"614da70a6c5523c9f320d8ef"},{"id":51611,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Continuity and Differentiability","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>→</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be a function defined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mo> </mo><mi>for</mi><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo> </mo><mi>for</mi><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math> The set of points where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is not differentiable is","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo>[</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></math>","{<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Z</mi></math>}","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>"],"answer":2,"solution":"<p>We have,</p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mtable columnalign=\"center left\"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mtd><mtd><mo> </mo><mi>for</mi><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo> </mo><mi>for</mi><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is not differentiable at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∵</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is not differentiable at</p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>Z</mi></math></p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2018 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"614da6a2ca5c4a1814a1e317"},{"id":51612,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Continuity and Differentiability","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>|sin</mi><mi>x|</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></math>. Then,","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is differentiable for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>, except at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></math>,","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is differentiable for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>, except at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is differentiable for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>, except at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is differentiable for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>, except at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo></math>"],"answer":1,"solution":"<p>We have, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>π</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>π</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p>\n\n<p>Clearly, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is differentiable for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> except <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo></math></p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2018 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"614da6a2138f915f5df0b093"},{"id":51613,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Continuity and Differentiability","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>→</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be a differentiable function satisfying <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math> for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> The number of such functions is</p>","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>","more than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>"],"answer":3,"solution":"<p>It is given that, </p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>∀</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p>Case <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> </p>\n\n<p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>∀</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p>Then, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></msqrt></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow><msqrt><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>∵</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∀</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p>Case <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> </p>\n\n<p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo><</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>∀</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p>Then, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></msqrt></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo> </mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∀</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"[\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo><</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo><</mo><mi>x</mi><mo><</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"[\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo><</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo><</mo><mi>x</mi><mo><</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"[\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo><</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo><</mo><mi>x</mi><mo><</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"[\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo><</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo><</mo><mi>x</mi><mo><</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo><</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo><</mo><mi>x</mi><mo><</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo></mrow></mfenced></math> and so on.</p>\n\n<p>Hence, there are more than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> functions possible.</p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2019 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"614da727fcc192f7e0bb7995"},{"id":51614,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Continuity and Differentiability","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Let $f:[0, \\pi] \\rightarrow R$ be defined as $f(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{array}{ll}\\sin x, & \\text { if } x \\text { is irrational and } x \\in[0, \\pi] \\\\ \\tan ^{2} x, & \\text { if } x \\text { is rational and } x \\in[0, \\pi]\\end{array}\\right\\}$\nThe number of points in $[0, \\pi]$ at which the function $f$ is continuous is :","options":["6","4","2","0"],"answer":1,"solution":"$\\sin x=\\tan ^{2} x\\sin ^{2} x=\\sin x\\left(1-\\sin ^{2} x\\right)\\sin x\\left(\\sin ^{2} x+\\sin -1\\right)=0\\sin x=0 \\quad \\sin x=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}-1}{2}x=0, \\pi \\quad \\sin ^{-1} \\frac{\\sqrt{5}-1}{2}, \\pi-\\sin ^{-1} \\frac{\\sqrt{5}-1}{2}$\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fkvpy%252FG8dfkKWnDZpmus7e2ZuRBJ837tb8nLHtK_zYuy7eEXk.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FG8dfkKWnDZpmus7e2ZuRBJ837tb8nLHtK_zYuy7eEXk.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FG8dfkKWnDZpmus7e2ZuRBJ837tb8nLHtK_zYuy7eEXk.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2014 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d2131b09c89e7bd17378"},{"id":51615,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Continuity and Differentiability","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Let $\\mathrm{f}: \\mathrm{R} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{R}$ be a continuous function satisfying $\\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})=\\mathrm{x}+\\int_{0}^{\\mathrm{x}} \\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{t}) \\mathrm{dt}$, for all $\\mathrm{x} \\in \\mathrm{R}$. Then the number of elements in the set $\\mathrm{S}=\\{\\mathrm{x} \\in \\mathrm{R} ; \\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})=0\\}$ is-","options":["1","2","3","4"],"answer":0,"solution":"$\\quad \\mathrm{f}^{\\prime}(\\mathrm{x})=1+\\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x}) \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})=\\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{x}}-1\\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})=0 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{x}}=1 \\quad \\mathrm{x}=0 \\quad$ One solution","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2010 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d21342f077fe95f7a084"},{"id":51616,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Continuity and Differentiability","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Consider the function\n\nf(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{array}{ll}\n\\frac{x+5}{x-2} & \\text { if } x \\neq 2 \\\\\n1 & \\text { if } x=2\n\\end{array}\\right\\}\n\nThen $\\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x}))$ is discontinuous","options":["at all real numbers","at exactly two values of $x$","at exactly one value of $x$","at exactly three values of $x$"],"answer":1,"solution":"$f(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{array}{ll}\\frac{x+5}{x-2}, & x \\neq 2 \\\\ 1, & x=2\\end{array}\\right.f(x)$ is discontinuous at $x=2f(x)=2$\n\\Rightarrow \\frac{x+5}{x-2}=2\n\n\\begin{array}{l}\n\\Rightarrow x+5=2 x-4 \\\\\n\\Rightarrow x=9\n\\end{array}\n","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2014 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d21366d1b177328e01db"}]}